  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through Sunday) \nIssued at 101 AM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nWednesday morning begins the final phase of this torrential downpour \nevent as numerical model solutions look to bring a dry slot punching \nin behind the remnants of Polo, favoring the southern half of the \nstate. Notable uncertainty remains regarding the dynamics around how \nPolo is absorbed into the H5 low over NM, either fully merging with \nthe low over northern NM or being ejected out over the High Plains. \nHow exactly this melding of systems plays will determine when \nprecipitation comes to an end for any one location. However it plays \nout, it can be said that wrap-around moisture will favor ongoing \nlower intensity showers over at least the northern half of NM \nWednesday, potentially lasting over western NM as long as Thursday \nmorning. Conditions looks to steadily clear west to east over the \nstate Thursday, with precipitation lasting over eastern NM as late \nas Friday morning. \n\nThe weekend finally arrives with clearer conditions and remnant \nhigh level moisture remaining in the form of higher humidity. \nRiver flooding and morning areas of fog are likely to linger over \nthe state during this time however.",
